course: dictionary
lesson: 5937
title: Mash: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «Paper is soaked, mashed into pulp and pressed into new paper.» The word pulp is your clue: mashed means crushed into a soft mass, not mashed potatoes.
explain: Read the sentence and ask: what would fit here? In «a lunchbox with everything mashed together», the clue is together, so mashed means squashed or mixed up in one lump. Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Mash can also be a noun. It can be food, such as mashed potatoes in «sausage and mash», or a soft mixture fed to animals. A mash-up is different again: it is a mix of two songs, videos or ideas.
fact: Mash means to crush food into a soft mass, for example with a fork or a masher.
fact: Mash can also be a noun for soft, mashed food, such as mashed potatoes.
fact: «Mashed» in «mashed into pulp» means crushed into a soft mess, the way paper is broken down to make new paper.
fact: A mash-up is a mix of two songs, videos or ideas.
fact: Context clues like «pulp» and «together» help you pick the right meaning of mash.
exercise: «Bananas can be mashed with a fork for a quick snack.» What does mashed mean here? | Cut into very thin slices | Frozen solid | *Crushed into a soft mass | Left to rot in the sun
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Paper is soaked and mashed into new paper» that means wet through in water. | *soaked | into | mashed | paper
exercise: Ben says a mash-up is a kind of potato. What is a mash-up really? | A cooking pot | A type of kitchen fork | A bowl of mashed potatoes | *A mix of two songs, videos or ideas
test: «A Year 3 story written as one giant block is like a lunchbox with everything mashed together.» What does mashed together suggest? | Packed neatly into separate boxes | Frozen in rows | Shared out fairly | *Mixed up in one squashed lump
test: In «sausage and mash», what is mash? | To crush with a fork | *Mashed potatoes | A mash-up of songs | A potato masher
exam: Mira says mash must always mean potatoes. Is she right? | Yes, because potatoes are the only food that can be mashed | No, mash only means to cook food in water | Yes, mash only ever means potatoes | *No, mash can also mean to crush something soft, a mix of songs or ideas
